dhesion-sports-basketball-nba-1-ac1 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_dah"></div></aside><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__hi"><div id=ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-high_impact-sports-basketball-nba-2-ac1 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_hi"></div></aside><div class=gnt_bc></div><gnt-bb></gnt-bb><div class=gnt_cw_w><main class=gnt_cw><article class=gnt_pr><div class=gnt_ar_lbw><div class=gnt_ar_lbl><a class=gnt_ar_lbl_a data-t-l=":section label|v|c|milwaukee bucks" href=/sports/bucks/ >MILWAUKEE BUCKS</a></div></div><h1 class=gnt_ar_hl elementtiming=ar-headline>Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks' 2021 championship run, NBA Finals</h1><div class=gnt_ar_by><a href=/staff/2648103001/christopher-kuhagen/ data-t-l=":byline with photo|o|c|text" class="gnt_ar_by_a gnt_ar_by_a__fi"><img class=gnt_ar_by_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/04/01/PMJS/89426717007-chris-kuhagen-032426.jpg?crop=2048,2049,x0,y0&width=48&height=48&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/04/01/PMJS/89426717007-chris-kuhagen-032426.jpg?crop=2048,2049,x0,y0&width=96&height=96&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" decoding=async loading=eager alt="Portrait of Christopher Kuhagen" fetchpriority=high data-t-l=":byline with photo|o|c|photo"/> Christopher Kuhagen</a></div><div class=gnt_ar_dt>Updated June 11, 2026, 8:15 p.m. CT</div><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em__fp gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527731007-gan-20210720-jhp-su-5-088.JPG?width=480&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527731007-gan-20210720-jhp-su-5-088.JPG?width=960&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" elementtiming=pg-lead-image fetchpriority=high decoding=async alt="Five years ago, Giannis Antetokounmpo led the Milwaukee Bucks to their first NBA championship in 50 years after he scored 50 points in the clinching Game 6 over the Phoenix Suns. It capped an incredible playoff run that also saw him return faster than anyone thought from a hyperextended left knee he suffered during the Eastern Conference finals. He would deliver several masterpieces throughout the playoffs and iconic NBA Finals moments. Scroll through this gallery for all of Giannis' highlights during the 2021 postseason."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Five years ago, Giannis Antetokounmpo led the Milwaukee Bucks to their first NBA championship in 50 years after he scored 50 points in the clinching Game 6 over the Phoenix Suns.<br><br>It capped an incredible playoff run that also saw him return faster than anyone thought from a hyperextended left knee he suffered during the Eastern Conference finals.<br><br>He would deliver several masterpieces throughout the playoffs and iconic NBA Finals moments.<br><br>Scroll through this gallery for all of Giannis' highlights during the 2021 postseason.</div>Mark J. Rebilas, USA TODAY Sports</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-3-ac1 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517361007-getty-1328783401-1.jpg?width=444&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517361007-getty-1328783401-1.jpg?width=888&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo blocks a shot by Phoenix Suns' Deandre Ayton in the closing moments of Game 4 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 14, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. The Bucks defeated the Suns, 109-103, to even the series."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo blocks a shot by Phoenix Suns' Deandre Ayton in the closing moments of Game 4 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 14, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.<br><br>The Bucks defeated the Suns, 109-103, to even the series.</div>Jonathan Daniel, Getty Images</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527750007-gan-20210714-neb-sh-5-197.JPG?width=572&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527750007-gan-20210714-neb-sh-5-197.JPG?width=1144&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second quarter against the Phoenix Suns during Game 4 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on Jul 14, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second quarter against the Phoenix Suns during Game 4 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on Jul 14, 2021.</div>Jeff Hanisch, USA TODAY Sports</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-4-ac2 data-x-c=2 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527699007-gan-20210619-gma-cc-1-1173.jpg?width=472&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527699007-gan-20210619-gma-cc-1-1173.jpg?width=944&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Milwaukee Bucks defeated the Brooklyn Nets in overtime in Game 7 in the second round of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center on June 19, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Milwaukee Bucks defeated the Brooklyn Nets in overtime in Game 7 in the second round of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center on June 19, 2021.</div>Wendell Cruz, USA TODAY Sports</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527769007-mjs-nba-finals-game-2-2.jpg?width=532&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527769007-mjs-nba-finals-game-2-2.jpg?width=1064&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) slams against Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) during Game 2 of the NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena July 8, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) slams against Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) during Game 2 of the NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena July 8, 2021.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-5-ac3 data-x-c=3 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527714007-mjs-bucks-25-5-jpg-bucks-25.jpg?width=280&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527714007-mjs-bucks-25-5-jpg-bucks-25.jpg?width=560&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) takes a moment before their first-round playoff series against the Miami Heat on Monday, May 24, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) takes a moment before their first-round playoff series against the Miami Heat on Monday, May 24, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee.</div>Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:440px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527710007-gan-20210529-gma-na-2-2317.jpg?width=660&height=440&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527710007-gan-20210529-gma-na-2-2317.jpg?width=1320&height=880&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) looks on in the fourth quarter during Game 4 in the first round of the 2021 NBA playoffs against the Miami Heat at American Airlines Arena. The Bucks beat the Heat, 120-103, to complete a series sweep. Antetokounmpo posted a triple double in the clinching game, with 20 points, 12 rebounds and 15 assists."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) looks on in the fourth quarter during Game 4 in the first round of the 2021 NBA playoffs against the Miami Heat at American Airlines Arena.<br><br>The Bucks beat the Heat, 120-103, to complete a series sweep.<br><br>Antetokounmpo posted a triple double in the clinching game, with 20 points, 12 rebounds and 15 assists.</div>Sam Navarro, USA TODAY Sports</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-6-ac4 data-x-c=4 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527698007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-173.JPG?width=529&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527698007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-173.JPG?width=1058&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) reacts during the second quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs against the Brooklyn Nets at Barclays Center on June 15, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) reacts during the second quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs against the Brooklyn Nets at Barclays Center on June 15, 2021.</div>Brad Penner, Brad Penner-USA TODAY Sports</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:441px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527692007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-222.JPG?width=660&height=441&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527692007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-222.JPG?width=1320&height=882&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks against the Brooklyn Nets during the third quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center June 15, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks against the Brooklyn Nets during the third quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center June 15, 2021.</div>Brad Penner, Brad Penner-USA TODAY Sports</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-7-ac5 data-x-c=5 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527713007-mjs-bucks-25-20-jpg-bucks-25.jpg?width=433&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527713007-mjs-bucks-25-20-jpg-bucks-25.jpg?width=866&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks the ball during the second half of their playoff game in their first-round series against the Miami Heat on Monday, May 24, 2021 at Fiserv Forum."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks the ball during the second half of their playoff game in their first-round series against the Miami Heat on Monday, May 24, 2021 at Fiserv Forum.</div>Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527691007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-116.JPG?width=529&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527691007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-116.JPG?width=1058&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) controls the ball against the Brooklyn Nets during the first quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs at Barclays Center on June 15, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) controls the ball against the Brooklyn Nets during the first quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs at Barclays Center on June 15, 2021.</div>Brad Penner, Brad Penner-USA TODAY Sports</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-8-ac6 data-x-c=6 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:621px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527739007-mjs-bucks-05218.JPG?width=660&height=621&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527739007-mjs-bucks-05218.JPG?width=1320&height=1242&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo takes a photo during practice at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Monday, July 19, 2021. The playoffs were held under COVID-19 limitations."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo takes a photo during practice at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Monday, July 19, 2021.<br><br>The playoffs were held under COVID-19 limitations.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:440px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527746007-gan-20210717-ads-su-5-019.JPG?width=660&height=440&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527746007-gan-20210717-ads-su-5-019.JPG?width=1320&height=880&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) attempts a shot as Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) defends in the first quarter during Game 5 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena on July 17, 2021. Antetokounmpo had a team-high 32 points in the Bucks' 123-119 victory. The win put the Bucks ahead in the series, 3-2."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) attempts a shot as Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) defends in the first quarter during Game 5 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena on July 17, 2021.<br><br>Antetokounmpo had a team-high 32 points in the Bucks' 123-119 victory. The win put the Bucks ahead in the series, 3-2.</div>Mark J. Rebilas, Mark J. Rebilas-USA TODAY Sports</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-9-ac7 data-x-c=7 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:440px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527688007-gan-20210625-gav-ma-9-061.jpg?width=660&height=440&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527688007-gan-20210625-gav-ma-9-061.jpg?width=1320&height=880&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) shoots the ball over Atlanta Hawks guard Bogdan Bogdanovic (13) in the first quarter during Game 2 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs on June 25, 2021, at Fiserv Forum."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) shoots the ball over Atlanta Hawks guard Bogdan Bogdanovic (13) in the first quarter during Game 2 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs on June 25, 2021, at Fiserv Forum.</div>Michael McLoone, USA TODAY Sports</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:645px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527740007-mjs-bucks-05094.JPG?width=660&height=645&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527740007-mjs-bucks-05094.JPG?width=1320&height=1290&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo gets iced up during practice at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Monday, July 19, 2021. He played through a hyperextended left knee during the NBA Finals."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo gets iced up during practice at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Monday, July 19, 2021. He played through a hyperextended left knee during the NBA Finals.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-10-ac8 data-x-c=8 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:415px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527729007-mjs-071621-bucks-5990.JPG?width=660&height=415&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527729007-mjs-071621-bucks-5990.JPG?width=1320&height=830&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) holds his NBA Finals trophy after the 105-98 win over the Phoenix Suns in Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) holds his NBA Finals trophy after the 105-98 win over the Phoenix Suns in Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee.</div>Ebony Cox / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527726007-mjs-071621-bucks-4526.JPG?width=478&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527726007-mjs-071621-bucks-4526.JPG?width=956&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second half of Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. Antetokounmpo scored 50 points as the Bucks defeated the Suns 105-98 to win the NBA championship."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second half of Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee.<br><br>Antetokounmpo scored 50 points as the Bucks defeated the Suns 105-98 to win the NBA championship.</div>Ebony Cox / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-11-ac9 data-x-c=9 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527696007-gan-20210627-ggw-sz-2-131.JPG?width=441&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527696007-gan-20210627-ggw-sz-2-131.JPG?width=882&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks over Atlanta Hawks guard Lou Williams (6) during the first half during Game 3 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs at State Farm Arena on June 27, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks over Atlanta Hawks guard Lou Williams (6) during the first half during Game 3 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs at State Farm Arena on June 27, 2021.</div>Dale Zanine, USA TODAY Sports</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:440px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527771007-gan-nba-finals-bucks-suns-basketball.jpg?width=660&height=440&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527771007-gan-nba-finals-bucks-suns-basketball.jpg?width=1320&height=880&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks for a basket ahead of Phoenix Suns forward Torrey Craig (12) during the first half in Game 1 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks for a basket ahead of Phoenix Suns forward Torrey Craig (12) during the first half in Game 1 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena.</div>Matt York, USA TODAY Sports</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-12-ac10 data-x-c=10 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527687007-gan-20210703-ojr-gb-1-200.JPG?width=441&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527687007-gan-20210703-ojr-gb-1-200.JPG?width=882&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (right) congratulates forward Khris Middleton (22) after a basket during the third quarter against the Atlanta Hawks in Game 6 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs on July 3, 2021, at State Farm Arena. Antetokounmpo missed the last two games of the series after injuring his left knee in Game 4."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (right) congratulates forward Khris Middleton (22) after a basket during the third quarter against the Atlanta Hawks in Game 6 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs on July 3, 2021, at State Farm Arena.<br><br>Antetokounmpo missed the last two games of the series after injuring his left knee in Game 4.</div>Jason Getz, USA TODAY Sports</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527705007-mjs-bucks-bucks-14-07469.JPG?width=646&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527705007-mjs-bucks-bucks-14-07469.JPG?width=1292&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) drive to the basket past Brooklyn Nets guard Mike James (55) during the 3rd quarter of their eastern conference semifinal playoff game at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021. Photo by Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel via USA TODAY NETWORK ORG XMIT: DBY1"/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) drive to the basket past Brooklyn Nets guard Mike James (55) during the 3rd quarter of their eastern conference semifinal playoff game at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021. Photo by Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel via USA TODAY NETWORK ORG XMIT: DBY1</div>Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-13-ac11 data-x-c=11 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:524px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527683007-bucks-02-30-jpg-bucks-02.jpg?width=660&height=524&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527683007-bucks-02-30-jpg-bucks-02.jpg?width=1320&height=1048&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Injured Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo congratulates center Brook Lopez (11) during the second half of Game 5 of the Eastern Conference finals game Thursday, July 1, 2021 at Fiserv Forum. The Milwaukee Bucks beat the Atlanta Hawks, 123-112, to take a 3-2 series lead. Antetokounmpo missed the game with a left knee injury. Lopez led the Bucks in scoring with 33 points."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Injured Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo congratulates center Brook Lopez (11) during the second half of Game 5 of the Eastern Conference finals game Thursday, July 1, 2021 at Fiserv Forum.<br><br>The Milwaukee Bucks beat the Atlanta Hawks, 123-112, to take a 3-2 series lead.<br><br>Antetokounmpo missed the game with a left knee injury.<br><br>Lopez led the Bucks in scoring with 33 points.</div>Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:440px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527727007-getty-1329800209.jpg?width=660&height=440&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527727007-getty-1329800209.jpg?width=1320&height=880&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo celebrates winning the Bill Russell NBA Finals MVP Award after defeating the Phoenix Suns in Game 6 to win the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 20, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo celebrates winning the Bill Russell NBA Finals MVP Award after defeating the Phoenix Suns in Game 6 to win the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 20, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.</div>Jonathan Daniel, Getty Images</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-14-ac12 data-x-c=12 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527732007-mjs-bucks-07657.JPG?width=649&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527732007-mjs-bucks-07657.JPG?width=1298&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) scores two of his game-high 50 points as Phoenix Suns forward Frank Kaminsky (8) tries to block the shot during the fourth quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. The 50 points are tied for most in an NBA Finals clinching game in NBA history."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) scores two of his game-high 50 points as Phoenix Suns forward Frank Kaminsky (8) tries to block the shot during the fourth quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.<br><br>The 50 points are tied for most in an NBA Finals clinching game in NBA history.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527737007-mjs-bucks-06523.JPG?width=558&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527737007-mjs-bucks-06523.JPG?width=1116&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) blocks a shot on Phoenix Suns forward Mikal Bridges during the first quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. It was one of five blocks for Antetokounmpo in the title-clinching game."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) blocks a shot on Phoenix Suns forward Mikal Bridges during the first quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.<br><br>It was one of five blocks for Antetokounmpo in the title-clinching game.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-15-ac13 data-x-c=13 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:493px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527715007-mjs-bucks-10780.JPG?width=660&height=493&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527715007-mjs-bucks-10780.JPG?width=1320&height=986&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks assistant coach Darvin Ham hugs Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo as part of the celebration of the Milwaukee Bucks' NBA championship in the downtown Deer District near Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Thursday, July 22, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks assistant coach Darvin Ham hugs Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo as part of the celebration of the Milwaukee Bucks' NBA championship in the downtown Deer District near Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Thursday, July 22, 2021.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:643px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527722007-mjs-bucks-08025.JPG?width=660&height=643&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527722007-mjs-bucks-08025.JPG?width=1320&height=1286&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates with Milwaukee Bucks forward P.J. Tucker (17) in the closing moments as the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates with Milwaukee Bucks forward P.J. Tucker (17) in the closing moments as the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-16-ac14 data-x-c=14 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527751007-mjs-bucks-13-3-jpg-bucks-14.jpg?width=411&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527751007-mjs-bucks-13-3-jpg-bucks-14.jpg?width=822&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="With his knees wrapped with ice bags, Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo watches the end of practice Tuesday, July 13, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, Wis. He managed a left knee injury throughout the NBA Finals but he didn't let it stop him as he averaged 35.2 points per game on 61.8% shooting."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>With his knees wrapped with ice bags, Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo watches the end of practice Tuesday, July 13, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, Wis.<br><br>He managed a left knee injury throughout the NBA Finals but he didn't let it stop him as he averaged 35.2 points per game on 61.8% shooting.</div>Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527734007-mjs-bucks-07502.JPG?width=516&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527734007-mjs-bucks-07502.JPG?width=1032&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Khris Middleton (22) and Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) talk during the third quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. Antetokounmpo scored 50 and Middleton added 17 in the game."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Khris Middleton (22) and Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) talk during the third quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.<br><br>Antetokounmpo scored 50 and Middleton added 17 in the game.</div>Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-17-ac15 data-x-c=15 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:573px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527777007-mjs-bucks-bucks-07-05049.JPG?width=660&height=573&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527777007-mjs-bucks-bucks-07-05049.JPG?width=1320&height=1146&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) warms up before Milwaukee Bucks play the Phoenix Suns at the Phoenix Suns Arena in Game 1 of the NBA Finals in Phoenix on Tuesday, July 6, 2021. Antetokounmpo returned to action just over a week after hyperextending his left knee in the Eastern Conference finals."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) warms up before Milwaukee Bucks play the Phoenix Suns at the Phoenix Suns Arena in Game 1 of the NBA Finals in Phoenix on Tuesday, July 6, 2021.<br><br>Antetokounmpo returned to action just over a week after hyperextending his left knee in the Eastern Conference finals.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527716007-mjs-bucks-10479.JPG?width=629&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527716007-mjs-bucks-10479.JPG?width=1258&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks Giannis Antetokounmpo holds the Larry O'Brien Trophy as part of the celebration of the Milwaukee Bucks' NBA championship in the downtown Deer District near Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Thursday, July 22, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks Giannis Antetokounmpo holds the Larry O'Brien Trophy as part of the celebration of the Milwaukee Bucks' NBA championship in the downtown Deer District near Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Thursday, July 22, 2021.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-18-ac16 data-x-c=16 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:441px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517165007-1319494750.jpg?width=660&height=441&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517165007-1319494750.jpg?width=1320&height=882&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo scores two of his 26 points  against the Miami Heat during Game 1 of their Eastern Conference first-round playoff series at Fiserv Forum on May 22, 2021. The Bucks beat the Heat, 109-107, in overtime on their way to a series sweep."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo scores two of his 26 points against the Miami Heat during Game 1 of their Eastern Conference first-round playoff series at Fiserv Forum on May 22, 2021.<br><br>The Bucks beat the Heat, 109-107, in overtime on their way to a series sweep.</div>Quinn Harris, Getty Images</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:504px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527690007-getty-1325147946.jpg?width=660&height=504&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527690007-getty-1325147946.jpg?width=1320&height=1008&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks' Giannis Antetokounmpo sets up a play against the Atlanta Hawks' Trae Young during the third quarter in Game 1 of the Eastern Conference finals at Fiserv Forum on June 23, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks' Giannis Antetokounmpo sets up a play against the Atlanta Hawks' Trae Young during the third quarter in Game 1 of the Eastern Conference finals at Fiserv Forum on June 23, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.</div>Patrick McDermott, Getty Images</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-19-ac17 data-x-c=17 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:472px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517164007-1319888888.jpg?width=660&height=472&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="