and point guard Kyrie Irving (11) during the second quarter of Game 1 in the Eastern Conference semifinals of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center on June 5. Antetokounmpo scored 34 poitns but it wasn't enough as the Bucks fell 115-107 in the series opener."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) drives to the basket against Brooklyn Nets point guard Mike James (55) and point guard Kyrie Irving (11) during the second quarter of Game 1 in the Eastern Conference semifinals of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center on June 5.<br><br>Antetokounmpo scored 34 poitns but it wasn't enough as the Bucks fell 115-107 in the series opener.</div>Brad Penner, USA TODAY Sports</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-21-ac19 data-x-c=19 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:653px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527704007-mjs-bucks-bucks-14-08034.JPG?width=660&height=653&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527704007-mjs-bucks-bucks-14-08034.JPG?width=1320&height=1306&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the fourth quarter of their Eastern Conference semifinal playoff game against the Brooklyn Nets at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021. Antetokounmpo scored a game-high 34 points in the Bucks' 107-96 win in Game 4 to even the best-of-seven series at 2-2."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the fourth quarter of their Eastern Conference semifinal playoff game against the Brooklyn Nets at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021.<br><br>Antetokounmpo scored a game-high 34 points in the Bucks' 107-96 win in Game 4 to even the best-of-seven series at 2-2.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:568px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527724007-mjs-bucks-07997.JPG?width=660&height=568&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527724007-mjs-bucks-07997.JPG?width=1320&height=1136&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates in the closing moments as the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals to win the championship in front of their home fans at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates in the closing moments as the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals to win the championship in front of their home fans at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-22-ac20 data-x-c=20 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:434px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527754007-mjs-bucks-13-2-jpg-bucks-14.jpg?width=660&height=434&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527754007-mjs-bucks-13-2-jpg-bucks-14.jpg?width=1320&height=868&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo, right, watches the end of practice Tuesday, July 13, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, a day before Game 4 of the series. Antetokounmpo managed a left knee injury during the NBA Finals after suffering the injury in the Eastern Conference finals."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo, right, watches the end of practice Tuesday, July 13, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, a day before Game 4 of the series.<br><br>Antetokounmpo managed a left knee injury during the NBA Finals after suffering the injury in the Eastern Conference finals.</div>Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527761007-mjs-bucks-12-18-jpg-bucks.jpg?width=611&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527761007-mjs-bucks-12-18-jpg-bucks.jpg?width=1222&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks the ball as Phoenix Suns forward Jae Crowder (99) looks on during the first half of Game 3 of the NBA Finals game 3 Sunday, July 11, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. The Bucks won 120-100 to get on the board in the series, the first of four straight wins. Antetokounmpo scored a game-high 41 points on 14 of 23 shooting, plus 13 of 17 from the free-throw line and 13 rebounds."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks the ball as Phoenix Suns forward Jae Crowder (99) looks on during the first half of Game 3 of the NBA Finals game 3 Sunday, July 11, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. The Bucks won 120-100 to get on the board in the series, the first of four straight wins.<br><br>Antetokounmpo scored a game-high 41 points on 14 of 23 shooting, plus 13 of 17 from the free-throw line and 13 rebounds.</div>Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><aside aria-label=advertisement class="gnt_x__c gnt_x__lbl gnt_x__ifg"><div data-g-r=lazy data-gl-method=llx id=~ad-slot-7103-wi-milwaukee-C1258-inline_flex_gallery-sports-basketball-nba-23-ac21 data-x-c=21 class="gnt_x_sl gnt_x_if gnt_x_ifg"></div></aside><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:660px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527717007-mjs-bucks-08750.JPG?width=475&height=660&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527717007-mjs-bucks-08750.JPG?width=950&height=1320&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.</div>Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel</figure><figure class="gnt_em gnt_em_img"><picture class=gnt_em_img_pt style=height:543px><img class=gnt_em_img_i src="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527719007-mjs-bucks-08096.JPG?width=660&height=543&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp" srcset="/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527719007-mjs-bucks-08096.JPG?width=1320&height=1086&fit=crop&format=pjpg&auto=webp 2x" loading=lazy decoding=async alt="Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. He scored 50 points on 16 of 25 shooting, as well as 17 of 19 on free throws, plus 14 rebounds and five blocks."/></picture><div class=gnt_pg_img_cap>Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.<br><br>He scored 50 points on 16 of 25 shooting, as well as 17 of 19 on free throws, plus 14 rebounds and five blocks.