r:#e0e0e0}.gnt_n_us_dd_ac{padding:0 15px 0 19px;border-left:1px solid #626262}.gnt_n_us_dd_lbl{margin:5px 0 0;color:#fff;font:700 12px/16px 'Helvetica Neue','Arial Nova',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}.gnt_n_us_dd_ba{display:block;width:192px;margin:3px 0 19px;padding:9px 1px 8px;border:3px solid #1665cf;outline-offset:-1px;color:#fff;font:700 14px/17px 'Unify Sans','Helvetica Neue','Arial Nova',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;text-decoration:none;text-align:center}.gnt_n_us_dd_ba__hl{padding:12px 4px 11px!important;border:0!important;background:var(--gnt-bc,#1665cf)}.gnt_n_us_dd_ba:hover{padding:8px 0 7px;border-width:4px;--gnt-bc:#0A32A0}.gnt_n_us_dd_a__li{margin-bottom:6px}</script><link rel=preload as=fetch crossorigin=use-credentials href=/global-q1a2z3lvOBJhMGFifw9np8mpEfVjPOqTU.min.json fetchpriority=low /><script type=application/ld+json>[{"image":[{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527731007-gan-20210720-jhp-su-5-088.JPG","caption":"Five years ago, Giannis Antetokounmpo led the Milwaukee Bucks to their first NBA championship in 50 years after he scored 50 points in the clinching Game 6 over the Phoenix Suns. It capped an incredible playoff run that also saw him return faster than anyone thought from a hyperextended left knee he suffered during the Eastern Conference finals. He would deliver several masterpieces throughout the playoffs and iconic NBA Finals moments. Scroll through this gallery for all of Giannis' highlights during the 2021 postseason.","copyrightHolder":"Mark J. Rebilas, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517361007-getty-1328783401-1.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo blocks a shot by Phoenix Suns' Deandre Ayton in the closing moments of Game 4 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 14, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. The Bucks defeated the Suns, 109-103, to even the series.","copyrightHolder":"Jonathan Daniel, Getty Images"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527750007-gan-20210714-neb-sh-5-197.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second quarter against the Phoenix Suns during Game 4 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on Jul 14, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Jeff Hanisch, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527699007-gan-20210619-gma-cc-1-1173.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Milwaukee Bucks defeated the Brooklyn Nets in overtime in Game 7 in the second round of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center on June 19, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Wendell Cruz, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527769007-mjs-nba-finals-game-2-2.jpg","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) slams against Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) during Game 2 of the NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena July 8, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527714007-mjs-bucks-25-5-jpg-bucks-25.jpg","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) takes a moment before their first-round playoff series against the Miami Heat on Monday, May 24, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee.","copyrightHolder":"Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527710007-gan-20210529-gma-na-2-2317.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) looks on in the fourth quarter during Game 4 in the first round of the 2021 NBA playoffs against the Miami Heat at American Airlines Arena. The Bucks beat the Heat, 120-103, to complete a series sweep. Antetokounmpo posted a triple double in the clinching game, with 20 points, 12 rebounds and 15 assists.","copyrightHolder":"Sam Navarro, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527698007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-173.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) reacts during the second quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs against the Brooklyn Nets at Barclays Center on June 15, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Brad Penner, Brad Penner-USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527692007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-222.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks against the Brooklyn Nets during the third quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center June 15, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Brad Penner, Brad Penner-USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527713007-mjs-bucks-25-20-jpg-bucks-25.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks the ball during the second half of their playoff game in their first-round series against the Miami Heat on Monday, May 24, 2021 at Fiserv Forum.","copyrightHolder":"Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527691007-gan-20210615-neb-ae-5-116.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) controls the ball against the Brooklyn Nets during the first quarter of Game 5 of the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs at Barclays Center on June 15, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Brad Penner, Brad Penner-USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527739007-mjs-bucks-05218.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo takes a photo during practice at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Monday, July 19, 2021. The playoffs were held under COVID-19 limitations.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527746007-gan-20210717-ads-su-5-019.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) attempts a shot as Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) defends in the first quarter during Game 5 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena on July 17, 2021. Antetokounmpo had a team-high 32 points in the Bucks' 123-119 victory. The win put the Bucks ahead in the series, 3-2.","copyrightHolder":"Mark J. Rebilas, Mark J. Rebilas-USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527688007-gan-20210625-gav-ma-9-061.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) shoots the ball over Atlanta Hawks guard Bogdan Bogdanovic (13) in the first quarter during Game 2 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs on June 25, 2021, at Fiserv Forum.","copyrightHolder":"Michael McLoone, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527740007-mjs-bucks-05094.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo gets iced up during practice at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Monday, July 19, 2021. He played through a hyperextended left knee during the NBA Finals.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527729007-mjs-071621-bucks-5990.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) holds his NBA Finals trophy after the 105-98 win over the Phoenix Suns in Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee.","copyrightHolder":"Ebony Cox / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527726007-mjs-071621-bucks-4526.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the second half of Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. Antetokounmpo scored 50 points as the Bucks defeated the Suns 105-98 to win the NBA championship.","copyrightHolder":"Ebony Cox / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527696007-gan-20210627-ggw-sz-2-131.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks over Atlanta Hawks guard Lou Williams (6) during the first half during Game 3 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs at State Farm Arena on June 27, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Dale Zanine, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527771007-gan-nba-finals-bucks-suns-basketball.jpg","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks for a basket ahead of Phoenix Suns forward Torrey Craig (12) during the first half in Game 1 of the 2021 NBA Finals at Phoenix Suns Arena.","copyrightHolder":"Matt York, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527687007-gan-20210703-ojr-gb-1-200.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (right) congratulates forward Khris Middleton (22) after a basket during the third quarter against the Atlanta Hawks in Game 6 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs on July 3, 2021, at State Farm Arena. Antetokounmpo missed the last two games of the series after injuring his left knee in Game 4.","copyrightHolder":"Jason Getz, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527705007-mjs-bucks-bucks-14-07469.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) drive to the basket past Brooklyn Nets guard Mike James (55) during the 3rd quarter of their eastern conference semifinal playoff game at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021. Photo by Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel via USA TODAY NETWORK ORG XMIT: DBY1","copyrightHolder":"Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527683007-bucks-02-30-jpg-bucks-02.jpg","caption":"Injured Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo congratulates center Brook Lopez (11) during the second half of Game 5 of the Eastern Conference finals game Thursday, July 1, 2021 at Fiserv Forum. The Milwaukee Bucks beat the Atlanta Hawks, 123-112, to take a 3-2 series lead. Antetokounmpo missed the game with a left knee injury. Lopez led the Bucks in scoring with 33 points.","copyrightHolder":"Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527727007-getty-1329800209.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo celebrates winning the Bill Russell NBA Finals MVP Award after defeating the Phoenix Suns in Game 6 to win the 2021 NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 20, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.","copyrightHolder":"Jonathan Daniel, Getty Images"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527732007-mjs-bucks-07657.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) scores two of his game-high 50 points as Phoenix Suns forward Frank Kaminsky (8) tries to block the shot during the fourth quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. The 50 points are tied for most in an NBA Finals clinching game in NBA history.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527737007-mjs-bucks-06523.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) blocks a shot on Phoenix Suns forward Mikal Bridges during the first quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. It was one of five blocks for Antetokounmpo in the title-clinching game.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527715007-mjs-bucks-10780.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks assistant coach Darvin Ham hugs Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo as part of the celebration of the Milwaukee Bucks' NBA championship in the downtown Deer District near Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Thursday, July 22, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527722007-mjs-bucks-08025.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates with Milwaukee Bucks forward P.J. Tucker (17) in the closing moments as the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527751007-mjs-bucks-13-3-jpg-bucks-14.jpg","caption":"With his knees wrapped with ice bags, Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo watches the end of practice Tuesday, July 13, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, Wis. He managed a left knee injury throughout the NBA Finals but he didn't let it stop him as he averaged 35.2 points per game on 61.8% shooting.","copyrightHolder":"Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527734007-mjs-bucks-07502.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Khris Middleton (22) and Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) talk during the third quarter of Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. Antetokounmpo scored 50 and Middleton added 17 in the game.","copyrightHolder":"Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527777007-mjs-bucks-bucks-07-05049.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) warms up before Milwaukee Bucks play the Phoenix Suns at the Phoenix Suns Arena in Game 1 of the NBA Finals in Phoenix on Tuesday, July 6, 2021. Antetokounmpo returned to action just over a week after hyperextending his left knee in the Eastern Conference finals.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527716007-mjs-bucks-10479.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks Giannis Antetokounmpo holds the Larry O'Brien Trophy as part of the celebration of the Milwaukee Bucks' NBA championship in the downtown Deer District near Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Thursday, July 22, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517165007-1319494750.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo scores two of his 26 points  against the Miami Heat during Game 1 of their Eastern Conference first-round playoff series at Fiserv Forum on May 22, 2021. The Bucks beat the Heat, 109-107, in overtime on their way to a series sweep.","copyrightHolder":"Quinn Harris, Getty Images"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527690007-getty-1325147946.jpg","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks' Giannis Antetokounmpo sets up a play against the Atlanta Hawks' Trae Young during the third quarter in Game 1 of the Eastern Conference finals at Fiserv Forum on June 23, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.","copyrightHolder":"Patrick McDermott, Getty Images"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517164007-1319888888.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo dunks the ball in the third quarter against Jimmy Butler of the Miami Heat during Game 2 of their Eastern Conference first-round playoff series between the Milwaukee Bucks and the Miami Heat at Fiserv Forum on May 24, 2021. Antetokounmpo had a game-high 31 points on 12 of 23 shooting and 13 rebounds as the Bucks crushed the Heat, 132-98, to take a 2-0 lead in the series.","copyrightHolder":"Quinn Harris, Getty Images"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527736007-mjs-071621-bucks-3219.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) lays the ball up while Phoenix Suns center Deandre Ayton (22) attempts to guard him during the first half of Game 6 of the NBA Finals Tuesday, July 20, 2021, at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. Antetokounmpo was unstoppable in the title-clinching game, scoring nearly half of the Bucks points in the 105-98 win.","copyrightHolder":"Ebony Cox / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527707007-mjs-bucks-bucks-14-07071.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) puts up a shot at the basket in the first quarter of their Eastern Conference semifinal playoff Game 4 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527709007-gan-20210605-gma-ae-5-0181.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) drives to the basket against Brooklyn Nets point guard Mike James (55) and point guard Kyrie Irving (11) during the second quarter of Game 1 in the Eastern Conference semifinals of the 2021 NBA Playoffs at Barclays Center on June 5. Antetokounmpo scored 34 poitns but it wasn't enough as the Bucks fell 115-107 in the series opener.","copyrightHolder":"Brad Penner, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527704007-mjs-bucks-bucks-14-08034.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks during the fourth quarter of their Eastern Conference semifinal playoff game against the Brooklyn Nets at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Sunday, June 13, 2021. Antetokounmpo scored a game-high 34 points in the Bucks' 107-96 win in Game 4 to even the best-of-seven series at 2-2.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527724007-mjs-bucks-07997.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates in the closing moments as the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals to win the championship in front of their home fans at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527754007-mjs-bucks-13-2-jpg-bucks-14.jpg","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo, right, watches the end of practice Tuesday, July 13, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, a day before Game 4 of the series. Antetokounmpo managed a left knee injury during the NBA Finals after suffering the injury in the Eastern Conference finals.","copyrightHolder":"Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527761007-mjs-bucks-12-18-jpg-bucks.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) dunks the ball as Phoenix Suns forward Jae Crowder (99) looks on during the first half of Game 3 of the NBA Finals game 3 Sunday, July 11, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. The Bucks won 120-100 to get on the board in the series, the first of four straight wins. Antetokounmpo scored a game-high 41 points on 14 of 23 shooting, plus 13 of 17 from the free-throw line and 13 rebounds.","copyrightHolder":"Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527717007-mjs-bucks-08750.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527719007-mjs-bucks-08096.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021. He scored 50 points on 16 of 25 shooting, as well as 17 of 19 on free throws, plus 14 rebounds and five blocks.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527725007-mjs-bucks-08339.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527741007-mjs-bucks-04962.JPG","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks assistant coach Vin Baker jokes with Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo during practice at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Monday, July 19, 2021, ahead of Game 6 on July 20.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527695007-mjs-bucks-24-18-jpg-bucks-24.jpg","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) talks with head coach Mike Budenholzer during the first half of their Eastern Conference finals game against the Atlanta Hawks Wednesday, June 23, 2021 at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, Wis.","copyrightHolder":"Mark Hoffman, Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527783007-gan-20210629-ggw-ad-1-180.JPG","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) and Atlanta Hawks center Clint Capela (15) fall to the floor as Antetokounmpo (34) is injured on the play in the third quarter during Game 4 of the Eastern Conference Finals for the 2021 NBA playoffs at State Farm Arena on June 29, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Brett Davis, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527685007-gan-20210619-gma-cc-1-0953.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) puts up a one handed jump shot over Brooklyn Nets forward Blake Griffin (2) in the second quarter during Game 7 in the second round of the 2021 NBA playoffs at Barclays Center on June 19, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Wendell Cruz, USA TODAY Sports"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527767007-mjs-nba-finals-game-2-45.jpg","caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) has his leg worked on during Game 2 of the NBA Finals against the Phoenix Suns at Phoenix Suns Arena July 8, 2021.","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/06/12/PMJS/90517362007-getty-1328784481-1.jpg","caption":"Giannis Antetokounmpo blocks a shot by Phoenix Suns' Deandre Ayton to preserve the lead late in Game 4 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum on July 14, 2021 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. It's one of the most lasting images in NBA Finals history.","copyrightHolder":"Stacy Revere, Getty Images"}],"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageGallery","description":"Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks' 2021 championship run, NBA Finals"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"NewsArticle","headline":"Giannis Antetokounmpo highlights during Bucks' 2021 championship run, NBA Finals","alternativeHeadline":"See all these iconic Giannis moments from 2021 playoffs, NBA Finals","shortHeadline":"See all these iconic Giannis moments from 2021 playoffs, NBA Finals","description":"Giannis Antetokounmpo led the Bucks to their first NBA title in 50 years when he scored 50 points in a title-clinching game in 2021. Here are highlights from his iconic playoff performance five years ago.","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/picture-gallery/sports/nba/bucks/2026/06/11/giannis-antetokounmpo-highlights-bucks-nba-finals-2021-playoffs/83545633007/","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.jsonline.com/picture-gallery/sports/nba/bucks/2026/06/11/giannis-antetokounmpo-highlights-bucks-nba-finals-2021-playoffs/83545633007/"},"image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527725007-mjs-bucks-08339.JPG?crop=2980,1676,x605,y359&width=1600&height=800&format=pjpg&auto=webp","height":800,"width":1600,"caption":"Milwaukee Bucks forward Giannis Antetokounmpo (34) celebrates after the Bucks won Game 6 of the NBA Finals at Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee on Tuesday, July 20, 2021","copyrightHolder":"Mike De Sisti / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel","cropInfo":{"16_9":"/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527725007-mjs-bucks-08339.JPG?crop=2980,1676,x605,y359","16_9d":"2980,1676","3_4":"/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527725007-mjs-bucks-08339.JPG?crop=2057,2742,x1164,y0","3_4d":"2057,2742","1_1":"/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527725007-mjs-bucks-08339.JPG?crop=2357,2357,x937,y80","1_1d":"2357,2357","4_3":"/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527725007-mjs-bucks-08339.JPG?crop=3659,2742,x185,y1","4_3d":"3659,2742"}},"thumbnailUrl":"https://www.jsonline.com/gcdn/authoring/authoring-images/2026/02/05/PMJS/88527725007-mjs-bucks-08339.JPG?width=1200&disable=upscale&format=pjpg&auto=webp","datePublished":"2026-06-12T01:09:14Z","dateCreated":"2026-06-12T01:09:14Z","dateModified":"2026-06-12T01:15:02Z","articleSection":"sports","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Milwaukee Journal Sentinel","logo":"https://www.jsonline.com/sitelogos/m-oc.svg"},"author":{"@type":"Person","jobTitle":"Digital producer","name":"Christopher Kuhagen","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/staff/2648103001/christopher-kuhagen/"},"keywords":["access:free","source:Milwaukee Journal Sentinel","ssts:sports:nba:bucks","sstsn:Milwaukee Bucks","type:gallery","tag:Milwaukee Bucks","tag:Giannis Antetokounmpo","tag:DOT optimized","tag:DOT authored","tag:WI Content Sharing","tag:Evergreen Content"],"isAccessibleForFree":true,"isPartOf":{"@type":["CreativeWork","Product"],"name":" - Unlimited Digital Access","productID":"jsonline.com:standard"},"metadata":"{\"id\":\"83545633007\",\"siteCode\":\"PMJS\",\"contentSourceCode\":\"PMJS\",\"ssts\":\"sports:nba:bucks\",\"type\":\"gallery\"}"}]</script><noscript><img src="https://www.jsonline.com/gciaf/prod/p?a=pageview&p=PMJS-TEALIUM-TANGENT&m=web&k=f14ebdd6-0569-4c64-af73-99937bc06379&s=noscript" style=display:none;visibility:hidden /></noscript></body></html>